### Signing key material — NEVER commit ###
#Private keys, certificates and anything resembling them. The tax API's signing
#key is the credential; leaking it means someone else can issue invoices as you.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
dev-certs/
certs/

#ONE deliberate exception: the vendor's published sample keypair.
#It is printed verbatim in the public RC_TICS.IS_v1.6 PDF (the certificate as the
#x5c of the worked example on p.13, the private key in the appendix), it expired
#on 2024-03-23, and it belongs to a fictitious taxpayer. It is committed because
#the byte-exact conformance canary must run on every clone and in CI — with SDK/
#ignored, the canary would otherwise silently skip and the suite would report
#green with its most important test missing. See backend/tests/vectors/README.md.
!backend/tests/vectors/sample_keypair/
!backend/tests/vectors/sample_keypair/cert1.crt
!backend/tests/vectors/sample_keypair/privatekey1.pem
#Encrypted profile store written by the admin panel
backend/instance/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

